/*****************************************************************************
    jitXret -- ISOLATOR. ONE value-returning callee, NO conjunction.
    2026-08-08.

    jitXand died 139 with two degrades naming E2 -- `return INSIDE AN INLINED
    CALLEE ... it would branch to the enclosing function's epilogue`. That
    fixture varies TWO things at once against the working jitXcall: it uses
    AND, and its callees RETURN VALUES. This isolates the second.

    THE ONLY DIFFERENCE FROM jitXcall, WHICH IS GREEN (ticks 2, 8 -> 22, one
    compile, degrade 0): the callee ends in `return`, and the driver consumes
    the returned value instead of reading a field the callee wrote.

        RED here   ->  the wall is A VALUE-RETURNING CALLEE (E2), and AND is
                       an innocent bystander. This is the one that matters for
                       genKantParse, because EVERY term function in the sketch
                       returns success or failure.
        GREEN here ->  the wall is the conjunction itself, and the term
                       functions are fine.

    A NEGATIVE CONTROL IS BUILT IN (H7). xrSink is the jitXcall shape -- same
    callee, same arithmetic, but writing a FIELD instead of returning -- and it
    runs first. If xrSink is green and xrDriver is red in the same binary, the
    return is the only variable left standing.

    ⚠ TWO testing() CALLS ARE NOT AVAILABLE (the sequential-state tar baby), so
    the control leg runs INTERPRETED and is asserted for VALUE only; it is a
    control on the code shape, not on the engine. The jitted control is
    jitXcall, in its own file, which is the shape that rule exists for.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (H2). Run under a wall-clock cap (H5).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitXret);
define
    xrIn;
    xrOut;
    xrTicks;
    xrCallee code={
        xrTicks = xrTicks + 1;
        return xrIn * 2;
        };
    xrSink code={
        xrTicks = xrTicks + 1;
        xrOut = xrIn * 2;
        };
    xrDriver code={
        xrOut = xrCallee();
        };
    ;

xrIn    = 4;
xrOut   = 0;
xrTicks = 0;
xrSink();
print "XR control (interpreted, no return): xrOut =" xrOut " (want 8)":;

xrIn    = 4;
xrOut   = 0;
xrTicks = 0;
print "XR fire 1 setup : xrIn =" xrIn " -- jitting a driver whose callee RETURNS":;
testing(xrDriver);
print "XR fire 1 result: xrOut =" xrOut " (want 8) xrTicks =" xrTicks:;

xrIn  = 11;
xrOut = 0;
print "XR fire 2 setup : xrIn =" xrIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "XR fire 2 result: xrOut =" xrOut " (want 22) xrTicks =" xrTicks:;

xrIn    = 4;
xrOut   = 0;
xrTicks = 0;
xrDriver();
print "XR interpreted  : xrOut =" xrOut " (the oracle -- want 8) xrTicks =" xrTicks:;

print "XR SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
